{
  "ipService": {
    "serviceUrl": "https://api.ipify.org?format=json",
    "name": "ipify"
  },
  "cloudflare": {
    "apiKey": "YOUR_CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY",
    "email": "your.email@example.com",
    "zoneId": "YOUR_ZONE_ID_OR_LEAVE_EMPTY_TO_AUTO_DISCOVER",
    "dnsRecords": [
      {
        "name": "yourdomain.com",
        "type": "A",
        "proxied": false,
        "ttl": 300,
        "id": null 
      }
    ]
  },
  "lastKnownIp": "",
  "logLevel": "info"
}

CONFIGURATION INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Get your Cloudflare API Key: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
2. Find your Zone ID: Go to Cloudflare Dashboard > website domain > General (copied from URL or settings)
3. For dnsRecords.id: Leave as null - the app will auto-discover records by name. If you want to specify, provide the record ID.
4. Replace example values with your actual credentials and DNS record names
5. The first run will update all matching A records to your current public IP
